milar pattern of dose-dependent loss of cell viability in response to CDDP was observed between the 5-FU-resistant cells and the parent cells. The results are expressed as the means &#x000b1; standard error of the mean (SEM) of the mean values from three assays. (b) Effect of cilostazol on <italic>phosphodiesterase 3B</italic> (<italic>PDE3B</italic>) expression of HLF and HLF-R10 cells. Western blotting revealed that the expression of PDE3B was unchanged by the treatment of cilostazol in the 5-FU-resistant cells and the parent cells. &#x003b1;-tubulin was used as the internal loading control.</p></caption><media mimetype="tif" mime-subtype="tif" xlink:href="cam0002-0040-SD1.tif" xlink:type="simple" id="d35e2246" position="anchor"/></supplementary-material></sec></back></article>